#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""install_authoring.py - PRESENT AUTHORING (wave 2), one installer.

Installs, in blueprint order, into a COPY of T_Industries_SIREN_v1.html:

  1. BUILD MODE   - the route chip strip becomes a labelled deck editor. A visible
                    "Build" button (and the B key) on the map bar swaps the bar's
                    centre cluster for [Add] [Keep this view] [Tidy up] [Slides]
                    [Done]; the chips wear thumbnails, a permanent remove control
                    and a drag cursor. state.map.curated stops mapSeedRoute
                    re-adding diagrams the author removed and stops
                    mapPresentationDeckIds appending every diagram behind the route.
  2. CONTENT SLIDES - cards grow kinds title|text|table|image|embed|doc|facts with
                    one sanitised rich-text body, edited in a real dialog (never
                    window.prompt), images stored outside `state` and carried in
                    the .siren export, video shown as an honest drawn poster, and a
                    real SVG layout engine behind the deck PDF.
  3. PRESENT ONE CHART - the toolbar Present button grows a caret: "Present just
                    this diagram" goes straight into that chart's walkthrough with
                    no Map detour, counts slides honestly and exits to the editor.

Usage:  python install_authoring.py <target.html>

Idempotent: a second run on an already-installed file is a successful no-op.
Anchor-guarded: every edit is found by exact current text; ANY drift aborts the
whole run WITHOUT writing. Atomic write (temp file + os.replace).
Refuses to touch the live file in Downloads.

Generated by _gen_install.py from fix_present_build.py, fix_present_cards.py and
fix_present_onechart.py, with mapAddCard / mapOpenAddMenu rebased where the Build
and Content waves collide.
"""
